# Build context for `Dockerfile.robozag` (robozag:dev). Shadows .dockerignore
# for this file only — the zag-root build uses Dockerfile.dockerignore instead.
#
# Note: this duplicates most of the entries in Dockerfile.dockerignore. That's
# the cost of per-Dockerfile shadows (no shared file to factor common rules
# into). Keep them roughly in sync.

# Heavy build outputs — must never reach the build context. Depth-agnostic for
# the same reason as Dockerfile.dockerignore: bare `target/`/`dist/` only match
# the context root, so nested build dirs (go-port/*/target, packages/*/dist)
# were shipped on every build.
**/target/
bazel-*
**/node_modules
**/dist/
runs/
.xwin-cache/
packages/coding-agent/binaries/
packages/natives/npm/
packages/natives/native/
**/.cache/
packages/snapcompact/research/results/
# The addon comes from ZAG_BASE; nothing in this context needs one.
**/*.node

# Per-host scratch the zag codebase uses for parallel agents / worktrees.
.fallow/
.worktrees/
.wt/
.opencode/
.zag_config/
.zag/plugins/

# VCS, editors, IDEs.
.git/
.npm/
.vscode/
.zed/
.idea/

# OS + transient noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp

# Logs + profiling artifacts.
*.log
*.cpuprofile
*.heapprofile
*.heapsnapshot
CPU.*

# Build / test side outputs.
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.nyc_output/
__pycache__/
compaction-results/
changes/

# Generated files (the in-image build regenerates them).
packages/coding-agent/src/internal-urls/docs-index.generated.ts
packages/natives/native/.build/
packages/natives/native/zag_natives.darwin-*.node
packages/natives/native/zag_natives.dev.node
packages/ai/test/.temp-images/
python/zag-rpc/src/zag_rpc.egg-info/
python/robozag/data/
python/robozag/.cache/
python/robozag/src/robozag/static/
python/robozag/web/dist/

# Scratch files the repo creates ad-hoc.
syntax.jsonl
out.jsonl
out.html
zag-*.html

# Host virtualenvs — the image installs its own interpreter deps.
**/.venv/

# Secrets. Should never be in the image regardless. Depth-agnostic: a bare
# `.env` misses `python/robozag/.env`, which sits next to the copied src tree.
**/.env

# Robozag-only excludes. Natives + wheel + python + bun + rustup all come
# from ZAG_BASE; the web-builder stage only needs root manifests + the
# python/robozag/web tree; the runtime stage only COPYs python/robozag/
# pyproject + src + entrypoint. Everything below is dead weight in the
# robozag build context.
crates/
docs/
assets/
scripts/
AGENTS.md
README.md
